(512489, 49033, 10818, '<td valign="top">No doubt my favorite photo in the contest.  I gave it an 8.  After looking at it a couple more times after I voted and the contest was over, well I should have voted higher.  Congrats, wonderful job.</td>', 'No doubt my favorite photo in the contest.  I gave it an 8.  After looking at it a couple more times after I voted and the contest was over, well I should have voted higher.  Congrats, wonderful job.', '2003-12-14 00:06:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(512685, 48515, 9906, '<td valign="top">From the Critique Club<br/> <br/>First of all, a disclaimer.  I didn''t enter this challenge because I could not get a good shot with the limitations of my camera.  That out of the way...<br/> <br/>The first thing I noticed about many of the Soft Focus shots were that they were VERY dark and DULL in color.  This one is no exception on those details.  However, with this shot I personally think that those issues are not as important.  This shot comes off good as dark as it is.  I WOULD like to see just a TAD BIT of fill light on the left and rear cactus parts.  Also, the dullness of the color here is not really a detraction because of the almost monotone color scheme!<br/> <br/>I am a little bit amazed that you maintained a sense of pokiness of the cactii thorns here.  Even though the focus is soft, the thorns still seem very sharp and something to stay away from!<br/> <br/>A very nice image overall and MUCH better than I could have hoped to achieve!<br/>TC<br/></td>', 'From the Critique Club First of all, a disclaimer.  I didn''t enter this challenge because I could not get a good shot with the limitations of my camera.  That out of the way... The first thing I noticed about many of the Soft Focus shots were that they were VERY dark and DULL in color.  This one is no exception on those details.  However, with this shot I personally think that those issues are not as important.  This shot comes off good as dark as it is.  I WOULD like to see just a TAD BIT of fill light on the left and rear cactus parts.  Also, the dullness of the color here is not really a detraction because of the almost monotone color scheme! I am a little bit amazed that you maintained a sense of pokiness of the cactii thorns here.  Even though the focus is soft, the thorns still seem very sharp and something to stay away from! A very nice image overall and MUCH better than I could have hoped to achieve!TC', '2003-12-14 11:11:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(512705, 48816, 6202, '<td valign="top">Critique Club<br/> <br/>This definately meets the challenge it is soft.  But for as soft as it is one thing stands out to me as just being to soft, the eyes.  With the dogs coloring and the soft focus you lost the dogs eyes.  I think had you been able to pull more detail around the dogs eyes the photo would have been outstand.<br/> <br/></td>', 'Critique Club This definately meets the challenge it is soft.  But for as soft as it is one thing stands out to me as just being to soft, the eyes.  With the dogs coloring and the soft focus you lost the dogs eyes.  I think had you been able to pull more detail around the dogs eyes the photo would have been outstand. ', '2003-12-14 11:53:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(512718, 48432, 7969, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the CC, the color in your shot are really great, certainly IMO the highpoint.  Matched by the intense look in your subjects eye, the focus and concentration are superb, I am curious if he is posed or naturally captured here.   The composition is very well done, creating a diagonal from bottom right (with leg)  to upper left (with arm).    The sharpness is certainly present, even though ''softened''.  <br/>I suspect if this shot was in a bocce ball magazine challenge it would win the ribbon.   I think the subject does not necessarily convey ''softness'', being a sort of burly dude :  ),  I do not tend to rate shots on topicality and while this one has been, softened, the feel of his activity is not soft really.  I think this is a very well done shot and my criticism is minimal in that it is very well done.  Keep up the good work, you seem to have a good grasp of the technical aspects of photography as well as an ability to capture some emotion.</td>', 'Greetings from the CC, the color in your shot are really great, certainly IMO the highpoint.  Matched by the intense look in your subjects eye, the focus and concentration are superb, I am curious if he is posed or naturally captured here.   The composition is very well done, creating a diagonal from bottom right (with leg)  to upper left (with arm).    The sharpness is certainly present, even though ''softened''.  I suspect if this shot was in a bocce ball magazine challenge it would win the ribbon.   I think the subject does not necessarily convey ''softness'', being a sort of burly dude :  ),  I do not tend to rate shots on topicality and while this one has been, softened, the feel of his activity is not soft really.  I think this is a very well done shot and my criticism is minimal in that it is very well done.  Keep up the good work, you seem to have a good grasp of the technical aspects of photography as well as an ability to capture some emotion.', '2003-12-14 12:16:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(512809, 49106, 7969, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the CC, I love the feel of this shot, it is wonderfully composed. They are whimisically placed, yet have a feeling of intention to them.   The larger number on them on the right, helps to weight your photo in that direction, making it very pleasing to the eye.  The reflections are also wonderful.  And despite this being ''soft focus'' the sharpness still shines thru.  The highlight of your shot is the foggy/silvery haze that hangs over it, giving it the feel of winter and chill. Your shot really does create a mood and a feel.  I think it is a wonderfully executed shot.  I am at a loss to tell you how it could be improved to be honest.  The calm and emptiness add to its beauty and simplicity. Excellent work!!</td>', 'Greetings from the CC, I love the feel of this shot, it is wonderfully composed. They are whimisically placed, yet have a feeling of intention to them.   The larger number on them on the right, helps to weight your photo in that direction, making it very pleasing to the eye.  The reflections are also wonderful.  And despite this being ''soft focus'' the sharpness still shines thru.  The highlight of your shot is the foggy/silvery haze that hangs over it, giving it the feel of winter and chill. Your shot really does create a mood and a feel.  I think it is a wonderfully executed shot.  I am at a loss to tell you how it could be improved to be honest.  The calm and emptiness add to its beauty and simplicity. Excellent work!!', '2003-12-14 15:22:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(512990, 48455, 2634, '<td valign="top">From the Critique Club :<br/> <br/>First let me say that I really liked this image.<br/> <br/>Soft focus was achieved perfectly, with subjects that worked well.<br/>Your composition was good, and lighting was also nice. <br/> <br/>You could have cropped a little more of the lamp out to keep it from overpowering the photo. I think one or two less items in the frame might have made it more effective too.<br/> <br/>Basically the shot fit the challenge well and that was reflected in your score and comments.<br/> <br/>Sorry, but the photo needs to be bad for me to have more to critique :)<br/></td>', 'From the Critique Club : First let me say that I really liked this image. Soft focus was achieved perfectly, with subjects that worked well.Your composition was good, and lighting was also nice.  You could have cropped a little more of the lamp out to keep it from overpowering the photo. I think one or two less items in the frame might have made it more effective too. Basically the shot fit the challenge well and that was reflected in your score and comments. Sorry, but the photo needs to be bad for me to have more to critique :)', '2003-12-14 20:48:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(513002, 49102, 2634, '<td valign="top">From the Critique Club :<br/>Great shot!<br/>As a flower lover and shooter, I can appreciate this one even more.<br/>Obviously by your score, your photo was well liked. <br/>You did a great job achieving soft focus without making the flower look blurry.<br/>Lighting and composition were good, especially the stem placed in the corner. You achieved a nice deep black background and picked a nice simple border to complete this.<br/> <br/>It''s hard to critique the good ones :)<br/></td>', 'From the Critique Club :Great shot!As a flower lover and shooter, I can appreciate this one even more.Obviously by your score, your photo was well liked. You did a great job achieving soft focus without making the flower look blurry.Lighting and composition were good, especially the stem placed in the corner. You achieved a nice deep black background and picked a nice simple border to complete this. It''s hard to critique the good ones :)', '2003-12-14 20:58:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(513008, 48856, 2634, '<td valign="top">From the Critique Club :<br/> <br/>Good job on your first set up shot!<br/>You did a great job with the lighting and soft focus here. Your choice of b&amp;w works well here.<br/>My only suggestions would be to have angled the book differently so we dont see the ucla stamp. I also would have removed the papers from the upper left hand corner. They make the layout a little busy and are picking up too much light(brings my attention there).</td>', 'From the Critique Club : Good job on your first set up shot!You did a great job with the lighting and soft focus here. Your choice of b&w works well here.My only suggestions would be to have angled the book differently so we dont see the ucla stamp. I also would have removed the papers from the upper left hand corner. They make the layout a little busy and are picking up too much light(brings my attention there).', '2003-12-14 21:06:20.000000', NULL, 0),
